                        "review": "It's good.\r\n\r\nIt's a bit weird, but it's good.\r\n\r\nFunctionally, this is a Banner Saga esque resource tracking game where your units die. But it's also a ccg roguelike.\r\n\r\nThe spin it puts on this is interesting. Your summons take chips of damage, which lowers their cost, drops their starting health, and can eliminate them from your deck if they get damaged enough. So everything plays kind of expendably. Chump blockers don't stick around long unless you keep spending resources at campsites to renew them. Of course, a unit that KOs a player loses its damage chips, increases its cost, and gets an upgrade. So there's a lot of flex to your deck even over the course of a single area.\r\n\r\nRuns, for their part, are solidly long. About 4~ hours on normal, which I cleared on my first try. Unlocks are mostly different ways of playing. New classes and cards. This isn't a roguelike you grind to win.\r\n\r\nWhich.\r\n\r\nDoes mean it might not have huge staying power unless you really vibe with the mechanics. I thought they were cool, but didn't love them enough to do another run.\r\n\r\nI think on sale, this is a really safe pick. It's good, approachable, solidly written, the art is nice. It wasn't lifechanging for me, but neither is a hamburger, and people don't usually regret spending ten bucks on a hamburger.",
